{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1426399-is-lethargic-condition-too-crippling","id":1426399,"title":"Is Lethargic Condition too crippling?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-27T17:20:29-08:00","id":1426399,"title":"Is Lethargic Condition too crippling?","content":"So, I just reread the condition and realized that I always played it wrong and not as it is RAW.<br /> <br /> By RAW, the penalty keeps stacking when you're awake, and every 6 hours you make a roll to fall asleep until the next sunset. <br /> You only resolve this after a full day's sleep.<br /> <br /> So if you stay awake to run some errands, and later you fall asleep, you awake next sunset, still with this condition. Which is all good, being tired the next night seems very appropriate. <br /> <br /> However, condition text doesn't differentiate between night or day, so on hour 6 of the next night, you are increasing your lethargic condition and making the roll (which is now penalized) or you'll fall asleep during the night, until the next sunset. If you're being really pedantic, you might be getting this roll earlier than 6 hours (like if you spent 5 hours awake during the day, then technically, after the first hour he &quot;completes&quot; a 6-hour awake cycle to tick up the condition.<br /> <br /> I always thought that the stacking up and rolls were meant to be happening during the day, and the next night you just walk around with whatever you accumulated. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-27T19:43:11-08:00","id":1426416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1426399-is-lethargic-condition-too-crippling#post1426399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, condition text doesn't differentiate between night or day, so on hour 6 of the next night, you are increasing your lethargic condition and making the roll (which is now penalized) or you'll fall asleep during the night, until the next sunset. If you're being really pedantic, you might be getting this roll earlier than 6 hours (like if you spent 5 hours awake during the day, then technically, after the first hour he &quot;completes&quot; a 6-hour awake cycle to tick up the condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>The penalty is cumulative based on how long you've gone without sleep. This is a fatigue mechanic \u2014 even if you wake up in a fashion that has you retain the Condition, you're not making a roll or incrementing the penalty to -1 until six hours into the night. The Condition is &quot;you're fucked up until you get a solid twelveish-hour nap&quot; and its mechanics funnel toward that outcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-28T03:31:08-08:00","id":1426442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1426399-is-lethargic-condition-too-crippling?p=1426416#post1426416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The penalty is cumulative based on how long you've gone without sleep. This is a fatigue mechanic \u2014 even if you wake up in a fashion that has you retain the Condition, you're not making a roll or incrementing the penalty to -1 until six hours into the night. The Condition is &quot;you're fucked up until you get a solid twelveish-hour nap&quot; and its mechanics funnel toward that outcome.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's not RAW, tho. RAW the condition text does not differentiate between night or day and keeps stacking up for as long as you have the condition even at night.<br /> <br /> Tho, I'm happy to go with that as RAI and just keep playing as I always was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-28T08:54:22-08:00","id":1426468,"title":"","content":"Do what works best for you and your group. Maybe there\u2019s a blood magic ritual that makes it work WAR if you want to mess with someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}